      "section": "frontmatter",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Introduction}\\label{sec:intro}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0012",
      "sha256": "2dcc65d6b9ec1151981432cc43cea0146a21157d689427db3a81d44063b071d8",
      "char_start": 3103,
      "char_end": 4228,
      "n_chars": 1125,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The representation fed to a clustering algorithm may matter more than the algorithm itself for unsupervised an"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0013",
      "sha256": "c22f47caa81ec7cb6e4f015d6066aac1603313f017df0685a53f3f1fc2583bbf",
      "char_start": 4230,
      "char_end": 4986,
      "n_chars": 756,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "A representation can carry information about a label and still fail to cluster by it. Linear separability and "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0014",
      "sha256": "ee5910f8d2619aaefab6fb1cad91396a31b48bd7ebc4dd1bd7de4d628b44ff3a",
      "char_start": 4988,
      "char_end": 6087,
      "n_chars": 1099,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The closest benchmark, by Filice et al.~\\cite{lookingbeyond2026}, compares ECG foundation models only with one"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0015",
      "sha256": "e38879612000213e66e135442fd40bd08aec9a7c66d776625e7489ccbe00fe46",
      "char_start": 6089,
      "char_end": 7909,
      "n_chars": 1820,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "We therefore compare five representations for the unsupervised separation of sinus rhythm (SR) from atrial fib"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0016",
      "sha256": "4afdec2dfaa41e91e84c8aeb37b136759effc3da5decf940f5cf2292f405ecda",
      "char_start": 7911,
      "char_end": 7952,
      "n_chars": 41,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Related work}\\label{sec:related}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0017",
      "sha256": "d3cfdbcb32c454790c460ec33585ff6e454e8c31b73bc3b7641bca5388e8159f",
      "char_start": 7954,
      "char_end": 9501,
      "n_chars": 1547,
      "section": "Related work",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{Unsupervised ECG and representations.} Hand-crafted features built from RR-interval irregularity an"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0018",
      "sha256": "ecb5be9d1e6c3eb5c14227365828330126e9b5d937cfd1ae6281cb22f8cf4747",
      "char_start": 9503,
      "char_end": 10170,
      "n_chars": 667,
      "section": "Related work",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{Clustering evaluation.} Cluster purity is not chance-corrected: assigning every point to the majori"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0019",
      "sha256": "b0f02f978fbe720133f9b494c5ffebe4791627431ff756caca709c81aaa43d43",
      "char_start": 10172,
      "char_end": 11160,
      "n_chars": 988,
      "section": "Related work",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{ECG foundation-model benchmarks.} Several recent studies benchmark ECG foundation models on supervi"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0020",
      "sha256": "97c51900aa383a58279e94ad550b22811a3dd3b28e0f9cd7b5222eff1e4b2a8e",
      "char_start": 11162,
      "char_end": 12015,
      "n_chars": 853,
      "section": "Related work",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{Closest benchmark.} Filice et al.~\\cite{lookingbeyond2026} evaluated frozen ECG foundation models a"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0021",
      "sha256": "58f73a85115cb870e9c901e9dc70be0c59b3ecfc2021a0b4dab3e2b59b522dd0",
      "char_start": 12017,
      "char_end": 12053,
      "n_chars": 36,
      "section": "Related work",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Methods}\\label{sec:methods}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0022",
      "sha256": "60e22f7e5d82d55f9882d00071eacee46dd55348b1c7a5117f04b8002a89a680",
      "char_start": 12055,
      "char_end": 12084,
      "n_chars": 29,
      "section": "Methods",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Data and cohorts}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0023",
      "sha256": "42756dad8820dd4f80925415b5d75d3a3118eb744598a13d67e1b035fc9bbac6",
      "char_start": 12086,
      "char_end": 12842,
      "n_chars": 756,
      "section": "Data and cohorts",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{PTB-XL.} We used PTB-XL, a public database of 10\\,s 12-lead records, whose data descriptor reports "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0024",
      "sha256": "ada05da07f3d220e5abbd2ba9ca9389770013482f8ee93a8134b4b7f37fe370b",
      "char_start": 12844,
      "char_end": 13871,
      "n_chars": 1027,
      "section": "Data and cohorts",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Rhythm labels were taken from the statements of the Standard Communication Protocol for computer-assisted elec"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0025",
      "sha256": "a10089fa5cb69185d01d55005dc57fedd269a3a560c5dc1f17949be1e050356a",
      "char_start": 13873,
      "char_end": 14393,
      "n_chars": 520,
      "section": "Data and cohorts",
      "first_line_excerpt": "We study this binary task because one clinical criterion defines atrial fibrillation. Atrial fibrillation is r"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0026",
      "sha256": "62420f8fe3e223c4dc09b240d5807042131f7fa0c7b2108982a14805205a3350",
      "char_start": 14395,
      "char_end": 15179,
      "n_chars": 784,
      "section": "Data and cohorts",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{MIT-BIH.} For generalization we used the MIT-BIH Arrhythmia Database \\cite{mitbih2001,physionet2000"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0027",
      "sha256": "91e4e2252c72a8cd819c7c8d185fb0b852b467bc889e68c5f638fa0e0c9a0a34",
      "char_start": 15181,
      "char_end": 15225,
      "n_chars": 44,
      "section": "Data and cohorts",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Representations}\\label{sec:repr}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0028",
      "sha256": "da0757a667f5a3efe4e4f49cb9e7853f508f26e4a6e89a597c3f2ef1849a82ac",
      "char_start": 15227,
      "char_end": 18439,
      "n_chars": 3212,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "We compared five representations on PTB-XL, and the conditioner of Section~\\ref{sec:clust} transformed each of"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0029",
      "sha256": "3b19ff36341def8f34304f42e1ea3a6a331f627be048dd05f36f43c19a250978",
      "char_start": 18441,
      "char_end": 19853,
      "n_chars": 1412,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Only the hand-crafted features used a single lead. Raw flattening reproduces the 12-lead representation of the"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0030",
      "sha256": "5dadc810a0b5d00c95d8d5be9c68e430e5bc616b0bf425512889e99c809778b8",
      "char_start": 19855,
      "char_end": 20491,
      "n_chars": 636,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "We chose the two foundation models by three criteria:"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0031",
      "sha256": "5f17ca0e18c7643506c280e92cbddef35006da08017fa848137aeae13af9d2f4",
      "char_start": 20493,
      "char_end": 21844,
      "n_chars": 1351,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "On MIT-BIH the rhythm features do not apply to single beats, so we compared three beat representations. The ra"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0032",
      "sha256": "5aeba33ed85ac4d289ce5e47cdedc941673fa48af8820da7851e6678f6fa2b1a",
      "char_start": 21846,
      "char_end": 23346,
      "n_chars": 1500,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{table}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0033",
      "sha256": "d3a8e6de26588dc31f3890eab8db5aadc275949286f94d0c1f3eed03012c3d23",
      "char_start": 23348,
      "char_end": 23403,
      "n_chars": 55,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Clustering and evaluation}\\label{sec:clust}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0034",
      "sha256": "3de83c3237c9c2b675f6ef7e584276abe443eec95103ab6736f4c359eb295566",
      "char_start": 23405,
      "char_end": 24697,
      "n_chars": 1292,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Each representation was clustered with five clustering algorithms \\cite{sklearn2011}: $k$-means, Ward agglomer"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0035",
      "sha256": "e45b8c8bd18b186a5fc4f9ec2778d13a77fee2509ff5af2cc95fa3f9c72599c4",
      "char_start": 24699,
      "char_end": 25511,
      "n_chars": 812,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The headline metrics are the ARI \\cite{hubertarabie1985} and the AMI \\cite{vinh2010}, which are corrected for "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0036",
      "sha256": "7a7f6fa24f9a55e424d21b2745a56998877b9ed6a0a6a95eb6a07aaca15e636e",
      "char_start": 25513,
      "char_end": 26500,
      "n_chars": 987,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "A supervised ceiling measures how much of the label a linear classifier recovers from the same representation "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0037",
      "sha256": "db79da675e5405b36eb90a1fa207a81eadb46b579a90c9dd9106d1e640c32cae",
      "char_start": 26502,
      "char_end": 27405,
      "n_chars": 903,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "In the main benchmark each fit of $k$-means, spectral clustering and the GMM was repeated over ten seeds. The "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0038",
      "sha256": "fb855890e9d13ad6ebe18774de0f4f5aa2cb6faca651a4450cd1f8f31e3c28e2",
      "char_start": 27407,
      "char_end": 27957,
      "n_chars": 550,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Because heavy-tailed features can dominate Euclidean distance, we swept four conditioners: the Yeo-Johnson pow"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0039",
      "sha256": "3d904bff334d4f71615baa84a8f16123c5fe912efa3f83ffabb3d809da7d3234",
      "char_start": 27959,
      "char_end": 28651,
      "n_chars": 692,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Two further analyses test settings of the main benchmark, each with one fit. We report the AMI of $k$-means fo"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0040",
      "sha256": "04feef30da29230b3da7c4be4d3921794ef9232f4f3fa9d39cb9e3b707786a1d",
      "char_start": 28653,
      "char_end": 31187,
      "n_chars": 2534,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{table}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0041",
      "sha256": "f0caebead29e5a1b34e7121932452bc3d463cd246ebe955db65d64d8f88cbf71",
      "char_start": 31189,
      "char_end": 33522,
      "n_chars": 2333,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{table}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0042",
      "sha256": "9d4976f410cdbad7019b2c94b740986782907e1507211b0674cc09b187abce23",
      "char_start": 33524,
      "char_end": 33568,
      "n_chars": 44,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Federated clustering simulation}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0043",
      "sha256": "83457bd6c4a0d5451514a666d202edbe44645371723f5cd5f8b1f36ec26daf36",
      "char_start": 33570,
      "char_end": 34919,
      "n_chars": 1349,
      "section": "Federated clustering simulation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "To probe deployment under data siloing we used federated $k$-means, with centroid aggregation in the manner of"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0044",
      "sha256": "38af922a42eab1675171bc8e32009b028472bf2fc5bbc7d98f5ff5312845354b",
      "char_start": 34921,
      "char_end": 34957,
      "n_chars": 36,
      "section": "Federated clustering simulation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Results}\\label{sec:results}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0045",
      "sha256": "f22d7c5177226ed2a271b44445b924bc3afb403f589104e20cba7d49ecd33056",
      "char_start": 34959,
      "char_end": 35014,
      "n_chars": 55,
      "section": "Results",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Clustering by representation and algorithm}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0046",
      "sha256": "5e9bd1ec31635c8713735bf17ccfdb0c6d6d65c80147ed5067164252881cb86f",
      "char_start": 35016,
      "char_end": 35701,
      "n_chars": 685,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "In the PTB-XL benchmark the choice of representation changed the ARI more than the choice of clustering algori"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0047",
      "sha256": "10a1a863b59c41597be18095be3fb8e64d5dd3471c9f27749a83c8277a705218",
      "char_start": 35703,
      "char_end": 37337,
      "n_chars": 1634,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{table}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0048",
      "sha256": "8192acd6000e1a4ad9f73eb31c2994bde626b388888266a75d11eaa610303f96",
      "char_start": 37339,
      "char_end": 37962,
      "n_chars": 623,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0049",
      "sha256": "4df46c604a95571871357bc157fa373569658f3359f49bff7be548829ce8f17b",
      "char_start": 37964,
      "char_end": 38790,
      "n_chars": 826,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The ranking of the representations did not come from the initialisation of the clustering algorithms. Across t"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0050",
      "sha256": "2621adee62141e0d4d2733cdbb37628616574183acdac9080f0c0296b45521e1",
      "char_start": 38792,
      "char_end": 39422,
      "n_chars": 630,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Two further checks agreed with the ARI ranking. The hand-crafted $k$-means partition had a purity of 0.901, ag"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0051",
      "sha256": "089f62f30ad52fbfa0dd96c44c7f8c3510cb36bf22bdbd148cb6ffd7f0e11e36",
      "char_start": 39424,
      "char_end": 40160,
      "n_chars": 736,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "HDBSCAN and spectral clustering gave low scores for most representations, each for reasons of its own. HDBSCAN"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0052",
      "sha256": "7259883e15e8319a9c7a55dc9523d68c38ce2c40fcdb54248f0a0521196b043a",
      "char_start": 40162,
      "char_end": 40221,
      "n_chars": 59,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Separability and clusterability}\\label{sec:sep}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0053",
      "sha256": "1fd3bad76b524f67f3052c82bee65b78002490a511e1993016e21a21627a04a8",
      "char_start": 40223,
      "char_end": 41548,
      "n_chars": 1325,
      "section": "Separability and clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The supervised ceilings (last column of Table~\\ref{tab:main}, Fig.~\\ref{fig:sep}) expose the gap between separ"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0054",
      "sha256": "0f04c6c88cdeecb085fdbfb9ca2880f8f02e21b4f334ba5ceace870ddd2d5aae",
      "char_start": 41550,
      "char_end": 42333,
      "n_chars": 783,
      "section": "Separability and clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "ECGFounder and the hand-crafted features both separated and clustered the classes, and we offer an explanation"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0055",
      "sha256": "830fd86009c537ec6c24f43e6809186f40ecbf79e7d7844535a4aa49006a96f5",
      "char_start": 42335,
      "char_end": 43215,
      "n_chars": 880,
      "section": "Separability and clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "HuBERT-ECG's embedding held the SR-versus-AF label, as its ceiling of 0.899 shows, but we read that label as l"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0056",
      "sha256": "c3780299413636034f77ac1654a39934df630d9ad463ac8ca56ebc5fb5602fc4",
      "char_start": 43217,
      "char_end": 43811,
      "n_chars": 594,
      "section": "Separability and clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Raw flattening and the conv-AE scored at chance for different reasons. With $k$-means, raw flattening placed o"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0057",
      "sha256": "86fa0ce89377cda597adc46fca22c8300f0842386b685f5102e1b760922b823b",
      "char_start": 43813,
      "char_end": 44746,
      "n_chars": 933,
      "section": "Separability and clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0058",
